---

Cramming the night before a quiz fades by Monday. One verse a day stays.

Open a doctrinal mastery scripture. Study it first — read the verse, sit with the key phrase. That phrase is the handle. When you hear it later, the reference should come with it.

Then Build: reconstruct the verse from tiles, once. You are not racing. You are seeing how the words fit.

Prove next. Type it with first-letter hints. Then type it cold, no prompts. The typed pass is what seals it for quiz day.

That is the whole loop. Tomorrow, a different verse. Teachers can share this same path without writing a new lesson.
